-- #1269 BYSTANDER FIXTURE -- "feature + UNRELATED code still behaves", the shape
-- AGENTS.md requires whenever a fix touches something that can affect names it
-- never sees (here: `oneImportIfaceMethods`/`filterIfaceMethods` in
-- `compiler/frontend/resolve.mdk`, which used to scope an interface's method list by
-- a PROGRAM-WIDE bare-name membership test instead of the actual per-import
-- provenance).
--
-- The graph DOES contain a collision: `gmod3.mdk` and `pmod3.mdk` both declare an
-- interface `Same3` at arity 1 -- one graded with required method `gandThen3`, one
-- ungraded with required method `pmth3`.  Only their unrelated FUNCTIONS are
-- imported here, so NOTHING BELOW MENTIONS `Same3`, `gandThen3` OR `pmth3`.
--
-- What the golden pins (every file's bucket is `[]`), and how each line could fail:
--   * `impl Solo3 ET` implements BOTH of `Solo3`'s required methods.  If
--     `oneImportIfaceMethods` still cross-contaminated (the pre-fix bug), this would
--     not actually change THIS impl's outcome -- `Solo3` shares no name with
--     anything imported -- so this line alone cannot witness the fix (see the
--     🚨 paragraph below); it is here so a totally unrelated interface still checks
--     clean.
--   * `impl Display ET` is a genuine BYSTANDER against the prelude, not a witness:
--     `Display` has exactly one required method (`display`), and this impl defines
--     it, so a miss and a hit are byte-identical (`None => []` vs `["display"] -
--     ["display"] = []`).
--   * `plain` mentions none of this fix's machinery at all -- it answers AGENTS.md's
--     "what happens to a program that never touches the table" directly.
--
-- 🚨 WHAT THIS FIXTURE CANNOT CATCH, stated so nobody reads it as covering more than
-- it does.  It detects a key that WRONGLY MEETS another module's row (a spurious
-- diagnostic appears where none should).  It CANNOT detect a key that never fires at
-- all -- both `checkImplIface`'s guard and `ifaceMethodsOf`'s first-match abstain
-- (empty list) on a genuine miss, so a write-side/read-side disagreement would leave
-- every bucket here `[]` and this fixture green while the checks had silently
-- stopped running.  That direction is covered by
-- `test/analyze_project_fixtures/1269_ifacemethods_genuine_rejects/`'s two cells
-- instead (one with no collision present, one with the exact collision shape here).
-- The pair is the assertion; neither half alone is.
import gmod3.{gdummy3}  -- ONLY the function; never gmod3's Same3
import pmod3.{pdummy3}  -- ONLY the function; never pmod3's Same3

interface Solo3 a where
  soloFoo : a -> Int
  soloBar : a -> Int

data ET = MkET

impl Solo3 ET where
  soloFoo e = 1
  soloBar e = 2

impl Display ET where
  display e = "ET"

plain : Int -> Int
plain n = n + 1

n : Int
n = gdummy3 (pdummy3 (plain (soloFoo MkET + soloBar MkET)))
